```sql
SELECT m.name, COUNT(*) AS march_loans FROM members m JOIN loans l ON l.member_id = m.member_id WHERE l.loan_date >= '2026-03-01' AND l.loan_date < '2026-04-01' GROUP BY m.member_id, m.name HAVING COUNT(*) > 3 ORDER BY march_loans DESC;
```

The half-open range (>= March 1, < April 1) is deliberate: it catches every March timestamp without depending on how many days March has. HAVING filters on the aggregate, which WHERE cannot do.

Result:

