```sql
SELECT category, product, revenue FROM (SELECT category, product, revenue, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY category ORDER BY revenue DESC) AS rn FROM products) ranked WHERE rn <= 2 ORDER BY category, revenue DESC;
```

A window function ranks within each category without collapsing rows the way GROUP BY would; the outer filter keeps ranks 1-2. (Ties would need RANK() instead of ROW_NUMBER() if both tied products should appear.)

