```sql
SELECT c.customer_id, c.name FROM customers c WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM orders o WHERE o.customer_id = c.customer_id AND o.order_date >= '2026-08-28') ORDER BY c.name;
```

NOT EXISTS is used rather than NOT IN so a NULL customer_id in orders could never poison the result, and it stops at the first matching order per customer.

